      "writtenOn": "2021-11-19T17:17:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m ok to do this, but are you sure you want it? This already represents a fairly tidy change that enables S4 residency (by watching SLP_S5) on Brya. I can see the rationale that there are technically two things happening in here (watching SLP_S5, and advertising S4 residency to the AP). But the two pieces essentially depend on each other, and if something were to happen it\u0027s nice to have a single thing to revert.",
      "parentUuid": "0cc7440f_cb68df89",
      "revId": "59a42b5c631594326f65fc7a23dcecbed5c1ac3e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0e89b031_73ca4e29",
        "filename": "include/power/alderlake_slg4bd44540.h",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 37,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-19T21:00:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I would prefer separate CLs for watching SLP_S5 in the ADL/ICL power sequencing and for enabling S4 residency on the board specific code.\n\nAny potential revert would only be on the platform files to disable CONFIG_HOSTCMD_ESPI_VW_SLP_S5 and CONFIG_POWER_S4_RESIDENCY.\n\nAlso, is this a valid combination?\n    CONFIG_HOSTCMD_ESPI_VW_SLP_S5\u003dy\n    CONFIG_POWER_S4_RESIDENCY\u003dn\n\nThe S4 residency feature flag explicitly disallows this:\n    CONFIG_HOSTCMD_ESPI_VW_SLP_S5\u003dn\n    CONFIG_POWER_S4_RESIDENCY\u003dy",
      "parentUuid": "2c79d9b1_609aa54f",
      "revId": "59a42b5c631594326f65fc7a23dcecbed5c1ac3e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d7b64451_bbaf57d0",
        "filename": "include/power/alderlake_slg4bd44540.h",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 37,
      "author": {
        "id": 1260470
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-19T22:17:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, I\u0027ll split them out. \n\nVW_SLP_S5\u003dn, S4_RESIDENCY\u003dn is explicitly disallowed because it is saying \"advertise S4 to the AP\", but we know from configs that the EC has no way to differentiate SLP_S4/SLP_S5, so transitions through S4 would always slide to their next state. In other words, we\u0027d be advertising something to the AP that we know we cannot do. (Note: If a GPIO_PCH_SLP_S5_L existed, aka a real line from the AP to EC for SLP_S5, we _would_ have to allow this combination, since S4 residency would be possible via the real SLP_S5 line).\n\nVW_SLP_S5\u003dy, S4_RESIDENCY\u003dn is technically a valid combination, it says \"wire up interrupts and report changes on VW_SLP_S5, but don\u0027t advertise to the AP that we can camp in S4\". It\u0027s not a particularly useful combination, but it isn\u0027t broken either. Maybe you\u0027d use it as a last-minute escape hatch if you wanted to stop the AP from trying to go to S4, but you didn\u0027t want to touch anything else.",
      "parentUuid": "0e89b031_73ca4e29",
      "revId": "59a42b5c631594326f65fc7a23dcecbed5c1ac3e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    }
